Subject: dark fiber redundancy

Harvey Newstrom:
> I would presume that any fiber carrier would have a mechanism to
> disconnect any connections that appear to jam with bad data.

When a telephone line is broken, disruption in service is generally not
major, because there are many redundant paths.  Active switching makes that
possible.  In a quasi-passive medium like "dark fiber", redundancy means
loops, loops mean echoes, echoes mean trouble -- loss of bandwidth is only
the beginning.

